@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
title Notification Methods class isolation boundary
component "AAA test" as Test
rectangle "Class SUT (one at a time)" {
 component "Real Notification Service\n(or LendingServiceImpl dispatch,\nor preference validation)" as Service
}
component "Sending Notification\n(delivery controlled)" as Mechanism
component "ReaderRepository double" as Repo
component "Recording NotificationService doubles\n(LendingServiceImpl tests only)" as Doubles
component "Fixed enabled set\nand fixed clock" as Fixtures
Test --> Service : inputs / assertions
Service --> Mechanism
Service --> Repo
Service --> Doubles
Service --> Fixtures


note bottom of Service
  "Notification Service" in this graph is a stand-in
  for the different implementations of
  NotificationService that will need their
  specific behaviour tested.
end note

note bottom of Mechanism
  "Sending Notification" is a stand-in for what would be the specific notification channel protocol (SMS, e-mail, webhook (https)).
  Delivery stays inside each implementation; how tests control it (framework client or local receiver) is pending. 0 real messages.
end note
@enduml
